course: dictionary
lesson: 16044
title: Winning words: victorious
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Victorious describes someone or something that has won. Look for the clue in the words around it: «The victorious team lifted the cup high.» Teams lift cups when they win, so victorious must mean having won.
explain: The word can also describe a shout or a smile that shows you have won. «The crowd gave a victorious cheer when the final whistle blew.» A cheer that comes after a win is a victorious cheer.
explain: Try swapping in your meaning to check it. «The army came home victorious.» If you put "having won" in place of victorious, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Victorious means having won a battle, game or competition.
fact: Victorious can also describe something that shows you have won, such as a victorious shout.
fact: Victoriously is the adverb: «She crossed the line victoriously.» It means in a way that shows you have won.
fact: Useful phrases: «emerge victorious» means come out as the winner; «victorious over» means beat someone; «a victorious return» means coming home after a win.
fact: Victorious is the opposite of defeated, which means beaten or lost.
exercise: «The victorious team lifted the cup high.» What does victorious mean? | Sitting quietly on the bench | Very tired after running | *Having won a game | Having lost a game
exercise: «The victorious army marched home through the town.» What made the army victorious? | It went to sleep early | *It won the battle | It lost the battle | It forgot its map
exercise: «The team played victoriously in the final.» What does victoriously mean here? | In the rain and mud | In a slow and tired way | *In a way that shows they had won | In a sad and quiet way
test: «They emerged victorious over the other school in the quiz.» What does emerged victorious mean? | They were sent home early | They ran away from the quiz | *They came out as the winners | They lost all their pencils
test: The crowd cheered a ___ return when the team came back with the trophy. Which word fits best? | lost | quiet | sad | *victorious
exam: Which sentence shows that someone has won? | The runner was tired and sat down on the grass | *The victorious runner held up the gold medal | The runner ate her lunch early | The runner lost her shoes at the start
